WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.920
- There are some surprisingly
healthy parts of foods

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.520
that we're just simply not eating.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.290
So let's take a look at the parts of foods

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:07.600
that you may have been throwing away

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.470
and not eating unnecessarily.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.820
And stick around to the end of the video

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.920
to see one food that you should never eat.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.130
Strawberries are one of my favorite foods,

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:16.963
but as it turns out,

00:00:16.963 --> 00:00:19.010
there's a whole lot of
health benefits you can miss

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.300
by avoiding the stems.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.200
Throw the entire berry into your smoothie,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.970
as the stems are rich in
disease fighting polyphenols

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:25.803
and minerals.

00:00:25.803 --> 00:00:28.180
They also contain tannins
that have low pH levels

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.710
and can actually help with digestion.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.880
Zest doesn't just mean
great enthusiasm and energy,

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.130
but it's also the outer
covering of citrus fruit

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.170
and happens to be rich in terpenes

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.070
that actually give our
bodies some protection

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.640
from cancer cells and
aging from oxidation.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.700
And it's not just the peel, but the pith,

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.030
the white part around the flesh,

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.270
it contains hesperidin, a phytonutrient

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.150
that has been shown to
lower blood cholesterol,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.973
reduce blood pressure and
decrease inflammation.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.730
Outermost part of onions.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.600
Know, the onion won't suck
toxins out of your feet.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.370
Give me the claims, hit me with them.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:02.870
It will clean your blood!

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:03.880
God, why am I so angry?

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.100
But you can boost nutrition of your soups,

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.100
stews and rice using onion skins.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.470
They're rich in quercetin,

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:11.590
a flavanoid that has anti-inflammatory,

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.740
anti-cancer, anti-allergy,
exercise improving,

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.380
brain protective properties.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.330
Just to name a few.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.320
Do aim for the red over yellow onions

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.060
to get more of that quercetin boost.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.560
Praised by the liver king himself.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.820
Liver is known as nature's multivitamin

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.990
as it's one of the most
nutrient dense foods.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.970
It's incredibly high vitamin
A in the form of retinol,

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.930
which is the already active form.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.360
It's a great low calorie
high protein food,

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.890
but again, make sure you're
watching your saturated fat

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.193
and cholesterol intake.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.340
Broccoli and Cauliflower stalks.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.173
Fun fact.

00:01:44.173 --> 00:01:46.280
Did you know, broccoli's
actually a flower.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.030
(audience gasps)

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.170
It's easy to look and
think that the green leaves

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.100
are the only nutritious
part of the veggie,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.690
but in reality, the stems contain

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:57.930
healthy amounts of antioxidants and fiber,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.430
just like the leaves.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.650
The Sulforaphane found
in the stems and leaves

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:05.003
actually has potential as
a cancer fighting compound.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.710
Watermelon is more than the
perfect summertime snack

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.910
because while the bright
red center is delicious,

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.620
the rinds are useful as well.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.020
Pickled watermelon rinds
are filled with Citrulline,

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.290
an amino acid that helps
relax and dilate arteries,

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.700
which can be good for your blood pressure,

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.270
workouts and even sex.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.750
And it has more fiber and potassium

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.853
than the actual inside of the watermelon.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.830
Eat your heart out.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.040
Might not just be an old saying after all.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.890
As beef heart has a
similar texture and a taste

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.060
to a fine steak, yet it's inexpensive

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.870
probably 'cause folks
are hesitant to eat it.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.380
But it's actually a lean piece of meat

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.140
with a low saturated fat content

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.480
in comparison to other meats,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.630
it is considered a high cholesterol food.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.240
So beware.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.140
Carrot tops.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.390
No, I'm not talking about
him, I'm talking about them.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.550
Remember the orange part

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.230
is actually the root of the vegetable

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.040
and the green leafy portion
which can be tossed in a salad,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.880
added to a salsa or a hummus

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.710
have six times the vitamin A
as compared to the orange part.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.410
Pineapple cores might
sound kind of off putting,

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:05.460
but hear me out here.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.580
The entire pineapple, core included

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.670
is a solid source of Bromelain,
a protein digesting enzyme

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.140
that has shown to have
incredible medical potential

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.880
from anti-inflammatory effects

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.170
to helping with fungal
and bacterial infections.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.100
It is a little less sweet and firmer,

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.140
but if eaten raw, it still
packs the same nutritious punch

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.630
as the rest of the pineapple flesh.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.020
There's nothing tongue
in cheek about tongue

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.100
or veal tongue anyway.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.830
While it may have a high
cholesterol content,

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.510
it is rich in zinc, iron and vitamin B12.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.820
Both iron and vitamin B12
help replenish nutrients

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.180
that are low when you're anemic,

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.010
while zinc is an important nutrient

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.140
to keep your immune
system in tiptop shape,

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.340
especially during a pandemic.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.550
Turns out banana peels are useful

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.473
for more than just Mario Kart.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.410
Eating a banana whole,
seems rather untasty,

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.380
but the peel does become thinner
and sweeter as it ripens.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.760
So maybe you can wait a few days

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.770
for the banana peel to develop some spots.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.370
Bananas are no own for
their high potassium content

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:04.440
with a fruit averaging
about 400 milligrams.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.130
The peel contains an additional,

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:08.140
almost 80 milligrams of potassium,

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.740
plus plenty of filling fiber.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.780
Banana bread actually
became such a huge hit

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:12.613
during the pandemic,

00:04:12.613 --> 00:04:14.700
and a simple way they
start using those peels

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.270
is just to throw them
into the banana bread

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.130
for a boost of fiber.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:19.340
Care about your eyesight?

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.940
Then you're gonna hear this.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.010
Beat greens contain two phytonutrients,

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.720
lutein and zeaxanthin,

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.490
which have been shown to protect against

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.120
age related eye problems.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.470
One study actually found that

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.070
people who ate foods rich in them,

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.210
were half as likely to get cataracts.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.050
If you're chopping the
leaves from this veggie,

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:39.230
then you're toss away more
iron per serving than spinach.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.180
Cucumber peels are yummy, healthy

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.840
and worth their weight in gold.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.350
Okay, maybe not that last part,
but the first two are true.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.790
Sadly, when you peel the cucumber,

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:50.800
you are lowering the vitamin
K content by about 56%

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.900
than if you were to eat it whole.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.820
And vitamin K supports bone
health and blood clotting.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:57.620
Just be sure to wash it well
to remove the wax coating

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.420
that's often applied to prevent
bruising during transport.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.450
And if possible, aim for the organic store

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.610
to reduce possible
pesticide contamination.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.190
Full kiwis, including the kiwi skin

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.440
have become one of my
go-to late night snacks.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.320
Do you scoop out the
inside with the spoon?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.380
Well, you're missing out.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.510
You can triple the fiber intake

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.790
when you eat the entire kiwi.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.440
Just make sure that you wash it well

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.350
and possibly go for the organic kind

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:24.500
to cut down impossible pesticide exposure.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.090
While it might make you sick
to your stomach to think about,

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.810
an animal stomach shouldn't.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.910
Tripe refers to the edible muscle walls

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.540
of the stomachs of animals
like cows, Buffalo and sheep

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.670
who have multiple compartments
in their stomachs.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:38.890
Tripe is low in calories yet
rich in protein, vitamin B12

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.750
and the mineral zinc and selenium.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.323
The one food that you should never eat.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.840
Although, if you swallow one whole,

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:48.070
I guess it's not that big of a deal.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.050
Cherry pits.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.050
Inside of them, if they are crushed,

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.640
there is a compound known as prussic acid,

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.210
which is essentially cyanide.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:59.270
So do not chew on cherry
pits, spit them out.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.103
Thank you.

